    {
      "_id": "c3b3e01355224214",
      "name": "Melusine's Song",
      "type": "power",
      "img": "icons/svg/aura.svg",
      "system": {
        "description": "<p>Named for the legendary (and supposedly fae) progenitor of the houses of Anjou and Lusignan, this power lets a Toreador sway others through song. If the Artisan can phrase her request in the form of a song, her words take on the weight of a nigh-irresistible command.</p><p><strong>System:</strong> The player states the suggestion she wishes to weave into the song and describes the song's nature. Everyone within earshot must resist or unknowingly submit to the request. The effect lasts as long as the Toreador continues singing or until the target leaves her presence; commands requiring the victim to leave the singer's presence can be resisted once more after the enchanting voice fades. Listeners outside the Toreador's immediate presence may notice something odd about the performance, though it registers as little more than an exceptionally fine one; other Toreador within earshot are immediately entranced. As a side benefit, knowledge of this power makes the character a superlative singer even when the power itself is not invoked.</p>",
        "source": "Libellus Sanguinis II: Keepers of the Word, Book One: Artisans (Toreador)",
        "discipline": "Presence",
        "level": "advanced",
        "challengeType": "social",
        "bloodCost": "2 Blood Traits and 1 Willpower Trait",
        "retestAbility": "Performance",
        "duration": "As long as the Toreador continues singing, or until the target leaves her presence",
        "activation": "challenge",
        "active": false,
        "prerequisites": "Presence"
      },
